<h1>Aaron Donald Un-Retires: <em>The 2014 Combine Profile That Still Holds Up</em></h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<span>📖 6 min read</span>
<span>🏈 Football</span>
<span>🔥 Breaking · Rams</span>
</div>
<p class="dek">Aaron Donald is coming out of retirement at 35 to rejoin the Los Angeles Rams, signing a one-year deal worth up to $30 million to pair with Myles Garrett on a defensive line that now holds five of the last nine Defensive Player of the Year awards between them. His 2014 combine profile — still one of the most efficient testing performances by a defensive tackle on record — is a big part of why 35-year-old Donald is betting he can still dominate.</p>
</div><div class="content">
