<p>Donald retired with three Defensive Player of the Year awards, 10 Pro Bowl selections, eight All-Pro honors, and a Super Bowl ring, widely regarded as one of the most dominant interior defenders in NFL history. He last played in 2023, recording eight sacks in what turned out to be his final season before stepping away.</p>
<h2 id="combine">The 2014 Combine Profile</h2>
<p>Donald measured in undersized for a defensive tackle at 6-foot-1 and 285 pounds at the 2014 combine — the kind of frame that typically raises red flags for an interior lineman. What silenced the doubts was what happened next: a 4.68-second 40-yard dash that stood as the fastest 40 ever run by a defensive tackle at the combine until Calijah Kancey broke it by one hundredth of a second in 2023. Donald backed it up with 35 reps on the 225-pound bench press — second among all defensive linemen that year — plus a 32-inch vertical jump and a 9-foot-8 broad jump that would be strong marks for players 40 pounds lighter.</p>
